/// Decompiled `alisia_stage1` (tempo 116.955444, bar = 128 ticks).
/// One performance: intro once, then the loop body forever.
/// Bar-major score: outer `ser!` of `bar!` bars, each a stack of
/// channel `track!`s in score order (melody (psg), lead (ym), lead2 (ym), arp (psg), arp2 (psg), harmony3 (ym), harmony2 (ym), harmony (ym), bass (ym), drums (psg)); every sounding
/// channel restates its voice (`#[rustfmt::skip]` keeps it).
/// Each `bar!` outlines into its own closure for parallel codegen;
/// Voice programs bind once as `let voice_*` variables (spliced
         /// bare, never inline); `seg_*()` phrases are bar-local repeats
         /// phrases stay `seg_*()` calls with one definition each; cross-bar sustains are `legato!`
         /// plus rest cover.
/// One generator fn streams the whole performance: intro `yield_!`
         /// once, then `loop` yielding the loop body forever. Voices and
         /// music read top-to-bottom in one flow; `gen!`/`yield_!` come
         /// from our vendored genawaiter (de-hacked for rust-analyzer).
